  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "Degraded bus insulation combined with a medium to conduct the current (water) resulted in tracking on the bus. The degraded insulation was likely a result of cracking in the original bus insulation (Noryl). The site did not implement an adequate long-term strategy to address a known degradation mechanism with original Noryl insulation... In addition, the installed configuration of the wall penetration did not match the original design and was not being maintained to ensure weather tight characteristics.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "degraded bus insulation + water ingress via non-conforming wall penetration causing electrical tracking",
    "provisional": true
  },
